What was taken, and where it went:

    design-thinking/SKILL.md                          -> references/direction.md
    design-system/SKILL.md                            -> references/design-system.md
    design-system/references/motion-choreography.md   -> references/motion.md
    deterministic-design/design-spatial/SKILL.md      -> references/spatial.md
    deterministic-design/design-ux/SKILL.md           -> references/usability.md
    design-philosophy/{SKILL,reference}.md            -> references/philosophy.md   (merged)
    SKILL.md (its three specific UI rules)            -> references/interaction-rules.md
    .../design-spatial/scripts/layout-audit.js        -> scripts/layout-audit.js     (verbatim)

What was changed, and why. The upstream bundle is seven sibling skills that cross-reference each
other by path; collapsed into one skill those references would dangle, so:

  * Every cross-reference was rewritten to this skill's layout.
  * Two upstream section numbers were wrong and are corrected here: design-ux cited the overflow
    gate as design-spatial §2 (it is §4) and Fitts/transit-time as §3 (it is §5).
  * design-system linked design-spatial as `../design-spatial/SKILL.md`, which was not its sibling.
  * References to five upstream rules that exist only in the author's own repository
    (restraint-rule, verify-outputs-rule, media-attribution-rule, motion-preference-rule) were
    replaced with the plain statement of the rule, since naming a rule nobody here can read is
    worse than stating it.
  * design-spatial named two companion artifacts, `asym.html` and `analyze.py`, which the upstream
    repository does not contain. The techniques are kept and now say they must be built.
  * The upstream entry skill's routing was dropped; this skill's SKILL.md is the router, and its
    aesthetic direction is Anthropic's original frontend-design skill, which was not replaced.
  * The two blocking gates (render-and-judge, measure horizontal overflow) were promoted into
    SKILL.md, because a gate in a file nobody loaded is not a gate.

The upstream discussion of the "generic AI mean" and the pre-existing skill's list of AI clichés
said the same thing twice; they are merged into one section rather than stated in both places.

